(Chapter 2: Cellular respiration) '
(Cells break down glucose to make ATP.) '
(Section 2.1 Glycolysis: glucose is split into two pyruvate in the cytoplasm, net 2 ATP.) '
(Section 2.2 Krebs cycle and electron transport chain: mitochondria produce about 30 ATP,) '
(oxygen is the final electron acceptor and water is formed.) '
ET
endstream
